    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d823">

                <pb facs="0945" n="933" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg933"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/30253: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-21">July 21,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received July 21—3:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1894. I have received following telegram from Archbishop of Toledo who is Primate
                    of Spain:<anchor n="35" xml:id="d823-f1"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I beg you to transmit to His Excellency the President of the United
                            States the deep emotion of the Spanish Catholic Episcopacy and people
                            over the bombardment of Rome,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d823-f2"/> asking
                            that a repetition which might endanger sacred places and venerated
                            monuments be avoided.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Please inform me promptly what reply I should make.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d823-f1" n="35" xml:id="d823-f1-content">
                <p>Archbishop Enrique Pla y Deniel.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d823-f2" n="36" xml:id="d823-f2-content">
                <p>On July 19 certain military objectives at Rome had been bombed by American
                    planes.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
